  "reason": "With zero completed experiments, the most informative first step is to establish a clean, minimal baseline. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest configuration in the space: one modality, one profile, a linear and well-understood encoder, no aggregation, and no fusion. This isolates the 'floor' performance of the pipeline. Every subsequent experiment—adding image modality, switching to learned encoders (scvi, scgpt), moving to multiprofile, or introducing fusion—can be directly compared against this reference to attribute performance gains or losses to specific design choices. Starting with the simplest model also reduces the risk of confounding: if a more complex configuration underperforms, we can rule out pipeline issues more easily. Under a tight budget, this single experiment maximizes the information gained per run by anchoring the entire search space to a known reference point."
